It is surprising that you observe a time difference between rpy and R 
for the code you are showing and for the same dataset (and presumably in 
the same conditions - that is you are not running a huge process while 
trying rpy but not when trying R). What you are doing is
evaluate R code in a string (just like you would in R).

There is hopefully enough to get you started in the section 
"Documentation" at http://rpy.sourceforge.net/rpy2.html

Best,


L.




