From gregory.warnes at rochester.edu  Mon Sep 28 17:38:23 2009
From: gregory.warnes at rochester.edu (Warnes, Gregory R.)
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2009 13:38:23 -0400
Subject: Re: [Rpy] Why rpy.r.t is not working
In-Reply-To: <366c6f340909270956w12fd7462v974c6134dd20f0a1@mail.gmail.com>
References: <366c6f340909270956w12fd7462v974c6134dd20f0a1@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <1CE2EA12D4199B40A2E3634BE60CC29C437621@ITS-EXC1.UR.Rochester.edu>

The problem is that the R object returned from
"rpy.r.matrix(range(6),nr=2)" is being automatically converted to a
python object before being passed to the transpose function.

The easiest solution is to turn off automatic conversion, and then
manually ask for conversion when you want it:

>>> import rpy
>>> rpy.set_default_mode(rpy.NO_CONVERSION)
>>> x = rpy.r.t(rpy.r.matrix(range(6),nr=2))
>>> x
<Robj object at 0x2a1b0>
>>> y = x.as_py(rpy.BASIC_CONVERSION)
>>> y
[[0, 1], [2, 3], [4, 5]]

-Greg

